From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: qcom: sm8350: add eGPIO support

On SM8350, TLMM pins 168-202 are eGPIOs: each pad can belong to APPS or
to an island subsystem, selected by bit 12 (egpio_enable) of its config
register, with bit 11 (egpio_present) telling that the pad has the
choice. The driver describes neither bit nor an egpio function, so
msm_pinmux_set_mux() never claims such a pad for APPS: a GPIO requested
on one of them is configured as an output and keeps reading back
whatever the other owner drives.

On the Galaxy Z Flip3 the NFC controller's firmware-download line is
GPIO 201. Driving it low through gpiolib left the pad high, so the
controller started in download mode on every power-up and never
answered NCI. With the pad claimed it drives low and the controller
comes up normally.

Describe the ownership bits as sm8450 does and add the egpio function
to pins 168-202, so muxing one of them to any other function claims it
for APPS and selecting egpio hands it back. The range is the set of
pads with egpio_present set, read from the hardware.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
